{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "OOP Development (Object Oriented Programming)"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about programming languages and OOP. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Make the result report from the analysis of the information system, based on the customer requirements, following established rules and protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through the appropriate use of simple pronunciation aspects, and grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic progamming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Participles within sentences in present and past."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">participles</span>< to convert verbs into nouns or adjectives.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Participles </span><br>  Participles are in <span class=\"strong\">present </span> and <span class=\"strong\">past </span>form. You can form <span class=\"strong\">present participles by adding \u2013ing </span> to the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I have many things to do, I need a <span class=\"strong\">helping </span> hand. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "As you can see in the previous example, by adding <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ing </span> to the verb <span class=\"strong\">help </span>, it becomes and adjective that describes the following noun, in this case, hand."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Past Participles </span><br>  To form <span class=\"strong\">past participles </span> you need to take into account if the verb is <span class=\"strong\">regular </span> or <span class=\"strong\">irregular </span>. If the verb is <span class=\"strong\">regular </span>, you just need to add <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ed </span> to the verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I have an <span class=\"strong\">updated </span> version of that programming language. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb update describes the noun version thanks to <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ed </span>. On the other hand, to form <span class=\"strong\">past participles </span> with <span class=\"strong\">irregular </span> verbs, you need to look for the participle form of the verb because irregular verbs don't follow a specific spelling rule. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I have a <span class=\"strong\">broken </span> computer and a bad internet connection. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the previous example, we use the <span class=\"strong\">past participle</span> of the verb <span class=\"strong\">break </span>to describe the noun <span class=\"italic\">computer</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tProgrammers developed a new programming paradigm called object-oriented programming (OOP).  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Programmers didn't have an inherent connection between data and procedures to work around it; that was the starting point."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Finally, in 1980, C++ appeared as an improved version of C language which was already a trend."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some other updated languages are PHP, Ruby, Object Pascal, Objective-C, Dart, Swift, Scala, and Common Lisp."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Imperatives to describe a process"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you have to give a series of instructions, you can use <span class=\"strong\">imperatives </span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to give instructions, you need to describe a series of commands. To do this, you have to start your command with the verb in its base form (without to).Take a look at the following grammatical structure:<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"strong\">Verb </span> + Noun + Complement </div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Examples:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Turn on </span> your computer.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Download </span> the files I sent you. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Install </span> those files. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Open </span> the program. </span><br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sure, ask me whatever you want to know.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Go to the library, ask Mrs. Smith for a book called Basics of OOP, and meet me after school. We can study together."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "approach "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a way to deal with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They put a lot of dedication into a new approach."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "tendency; the way most people do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Finally, in 1980, C++ appeared as an improved version of C language which was already a trend."}, 