ts": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giving Some Instructions to Work with OOP"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the correct words to complete the presentation."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 9}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob04re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " OOP examples"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le02ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Hello, Nathan. What do you have there?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: Hey, Marry. It's an article about the development of object-oriented programming languages. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Just what I need! Can I ask you some questions about that? I need to study for a test. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: Sure, ask me whatever you want to know.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Why did programmers develop object-oriented programming languages? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: Well, in previous programming languages, programmers didn't have an inherent connection between data and procedures to work around it; that was the starting point. So, they put a lot of dedication into a new approach. Fortunately, their efforts paid off. Programmers developed a new programming paradigm called object-oriented programming (OOP)."}, {"time": "44500", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: I see. What did they do with OOP?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: With OOP, they could see an object as a whole; something with properties such as size and capabilities such as functions. That was more helpful than mixing up the capabilities and properties of various objects. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Interesting. What was the first programming language they developed?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: According to the records, it was Simula 67. They developed it in the late 1960s. Then, they launched Smalltalk in 1970. Finally, in 1980, C++ appeared as an improved version of C language which was already a trend."}, {"time": "86000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: What are some of the most common object-oriented programming languages nowadays?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: The most common are C++, Delphi, Java, and Python. Some other updated languages are PHP, Ruby, Object Pascal, Objective-C, Dart, Swift, Scala, and Common Lisp. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Wow, it seems that the development of OOP made history. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: Totally. The way programmers view data structures and functions changed since the development of object-oriented languages.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: Thanks a lot, Nathan. One last thing. What can I do to know as much as you do about OOP?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Nathan</span>: Well, go to the library, ask Mrs. Smith for a book called Basics of OOP, and meet me after school. We can study together."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le02ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [{"type": "template_override", "content": 1}], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}